  "summary": "The use of stenciled patterns or templates projected through lighting fixtures to create textured light effects on stage and surfaces.",
  "description": "Gobos create intricate patterns and textures through cut metal or glass templates placed in lighting instruments, transforming simple beams into complex visual elements. This technique emerged from early theatrical lighting innovations and became fundamental in creating atmospheric depth and visual interest in stage productions.",
